    "info": {
      "schema": "tgm.deviceinfo/1",
      "source": "waldorf-press",
      "text": {
        "de": {
          "description": "Der Waldorf Wave ist ein klassischer Wavetable-Synthesizer aus den frühen 1990ern. Die Unterlagen im Archiv sind die SysEx-Beschreibung (Operating System 1.400, September 1993) und die MIDI-Implementationstabelle (Version 1.640, April 1995). Er arbeitet mit Sound-Programmen und Performances in zwei Bänken zu je 128 Plätzen. Bis zu acht Instrumente und acht externe Geräte lassen sich in einer Performance mischen.",
          "features": [
            "Zwei Oszillatoren mit Wavetable, 128 Wavetables, Waves 0-299 im ROM",
            "Filter-Modi Tiefpass, Hochpass, Bandpass und Dual",
            "Vier Hüllkurven: Volume, Filter, Wave (8 Punkte) und Free (4 Punkte), dazu zwei LFOs",
            "Steuer-Module wie Ramp, Mixer, Delay, Shaper, Sample & Hold und Komparator",
            "Glide-Modi Porta und Gliss, auch MIDI-gesteuert und fingered",
            "Performances mit 8 Instrumenten, 8 externen Geräten, 8 Fadern, Free Wheel, Tasten und Pedalen",
            "MIDI-Tuning-Standard, wählbare Tuning- und Velocity-Tabellen",
            "SysEx-Dumps für Sounds, Performances, Waves, Tabellen und Global-Parameter"
          ]
        },
        "en": {
          "description": "The Waldorf Wave is a classic wavetable synthesizer from the early 1990s. The material in the share is the SysEx description (operating system 1.400, September 1993) and the MIDI implementation chart (version 1.640, April 1995). It works with sound programs and performances in two banks of 128 slots each. A performance can combine up to eight instruments and eight external devices.",
          "features": [
            "Two oscillators with wavetables, 128 wavetables, ROM waves 0-299",
            "Filter modes lowpass, highpass, bandpass and dual",
            "Four envelopes: volume, filter, wave (8 points) and free (4 points), plus two LFOs",
            "Control modules such as ramp, mixer, delay, shaper, sample & hold and comparator",
            "Glide modes porta and gliss, also MIDI-controlled and fingered",
            "Performances with 8 instruments, 8 external devices, 8 faders, free wheel, buttons and pedals",
            "MIDI Tuning Standard, selectable tuning and velocity tables",
            "SysEx dumps for sounds, performances, waves, tables and global parameters"
          ]
        }
      },
